{
 "_about": "Garmin's activity-type catalogue, every entry decided (RFC 0073). Pulled with get_activity_types() by the workflow's `catalogue` input. Each type carries exactly one of cardio (a cardio_sessions.activity_type, or by_name for hiit), sport (a sport_types.name) or skip (a key into reasons). A type Garmin adds later is in none: the sync skips it and warns, and it is decided here.",
 "pulled": "2026-09-30",
 "reasons": {
  "walking": "Walking-type: neither a cardio modality nor a sport in the app. Decided 2026-09-06; the reason corrected 2026-09-27 (RFC 0073). Hiking is the closer call and comes back only with a stronger reason than that it was recorded.",
  "strength": "Garmin's summary has no sets or reps, so there is nothing to put in session_sets, and its Training Effect is HR noise.",
  "mobility": "Mobility has its own capture, and this sync writes only cardio and sport rows. Syncing it is a separate question (RFC 0083).",
  "not_training": "No training stimulus the app reads: motorsport and vehicles, flying, fishing and boating, diving, timers and step counts, stillness practices.",
  "safety": "A safety alert, not an activity.",
  "category": "A category in the catalogue, not an activity.",
  "multisport": "A multisport container or a transition between legs; it carries no session of its own. How a triathlon's legs arrive from Garmin is unverified, because none has been recorded.",
  "unspecified": "Garmin's generic 'Other': nothing says what it was, so nothing decides where it lands."
 },
